.SH NAME
improv-functions \- the built-in functions of Improv formulas
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every built-in function, by category. Names are case-insensitive;
\fB[x]\fR is optional (\fB[x=1]\fR: 1 if omitted), \fB\[u2026]\fR repeats the
arguments before it, \fBx OVER T\fR is reduced over a category and
\fBINTO K\fR lays a list result along one. Positions are
1-based. An error argument (\fB#DIV/0!\fR, \fB#N/A\fR, \[u2026]) makes the result
that error, except in the functions that test for errors. See
The Formula Language for operators, types and
dimensions.
.SH "AGGREGATIONS"
Written \fBF(Measure OVER Category)\fR: collapse one category. Each also has a scalar form over its arguments, listed under its category.
.TP
\fBSUM(values OVER T)\fR \(-> number
the sum over a category (also \fBDSUM\fR)
.TP
\fBAVERAGE(values OVER T)\fR \(-> number
the mean over a category (also \fBAVG\fR, \fBDAVERAGE\fR)
.TP
\fBMIN(values OVER T)\fR \(-> number
the smallest value over a category (also \fBDMIN\fR)
.TP
\fBMAX(values OVER T)\fR \(-> number
the largest value over a category (also \fBDMAX\fR)
.TP
\fBPRODUCT(values OVER T)\fR \(-> number
the product over a category (also \fBDPRODUCT\fR)
.TP
\fBSUMSQ(values OVER T)\fR \(-> number
the sum of squares over a category
.TP
\fBAND(values OVER T)\fR \(-> boolean
whether every value over a category is true
.TP
\fBOR(values OVER T)\fR \(-> boolean
whether any value over a category is true
.TP
\fBXOR(values OVER T)\fR \(-> boolean
whether an odd number of values over a category are true
.TP
\fBFIRST(values OVER T)\fR \(-> the branches' type
the value at the first item (in category order) that has one
.TP
\fBLAST(values OVER T)\fR \(-> the branches' type
the value at the last item that has one
.TP
\fBS(values OVER T)\fR \(-> text
the first value, as text (Quantrix)
.TP
\fBTEXTJOIN(delimiter, ignore_empty, values OVER T)\fR \(-> text
the values in item order joined by the delimiter (skipping empty text when ignore_empty is TRUE)
.SH "LOGICAL"
\fBIF\fR and the functions built on it evaluate only the branch they choose, so an error or missing cell in the other branch does not matter.
.TP
\fBAND(logical1, \[u2026])\fR \(-> boolean
whether every argument is true
.TP
\fBOR(logical1, \[u2026])\fR \(-> boolean
whether any argument is true
.TP
\fBXOR(logical1, \[u2026])\fR \(-> boolean
whether an odd number of arguments are true
.TP
\fBIF(logical_test, value_if_true, [value_if_false])\fR \(-> the branches' type
then where the test is true, else (or no cell) where it is false
.TP
\fBIFS(logical_test1, value_if_true1, \[u2026])\fR \(-> the branches' type
the value paired with the first true test
.TP
\fBSWITCH(expression, value1, result1, \[u2026], [default])\fR \(-> the branches' type
the result paired with the first value equal to the expression, else the default
.TP
\fBCHOOSE(index_num, value1, \[u2026])\fR \(-> the branches' type
the index_num-th value (1-based)
.TP
\fBIFERROR(value, value_if_error)\fR \(-> the branches' type
the value, or the alternative where it is an error
.TP
\fBIFNA(value, value_if_na)\fR \(-> the branches' type
the value, or the alternative where it is #N/A
.TP
\fBCLEARERROR(value, [alternative])\fR \(-> the branches' type
the value, or the alternative (or no cell) where it is an error
.TP
\fBCLEARZERO(value, [alternative])\fR \(-> number
the value, or the alternative (or no cell) where it is zero
.TP
\fBCOALESCE(value1, \[u2026], default)\fR \(-> the branches' type
a cell wherever any argument that reads a measure has one: the first argument with a cell, else the last (the default)
.TP
\fBBETWEEN(x, low, high, [inclusive])\fR \(-> boolean
whether low \[u2264] x \[u2264] high (strict when inclusive is FALSE)
.TP
\fBTRUE()\fR \(-> boolean
TRUE
.TP
\fBFALSE()\fR \(-> boolean
FALSE
.TP
\fBSCAN(initial_value, array OVER T, lambda)\fR \(-> the branches' type
SCAN(initial_value, array OVER T, LAMBDA(acc, v, body)): the running fold along T, one value per item
.TP
\fBREDUCE(initial_value, array OVER T, lambda)\fR \(-> the branches' type
REDUCE(initial_value, array OVER T, LAMBDA(acc, v, body)): the fold's last value
.TP
\fBLET(name, value, \[u2026], body)\fR \(-> the branches' type
LET(name, value, \[u2026], body): the body with each name bound to its value
.TP
\fBLAMBDA(p, \[u2026], body)\fR \(-> the branches' type
LAMBDA(p, \[u2026], body): a function of its parameters, called on the spot or passed to MAP, REDUCE or SCAN
.TP
\fBMAKEARRAY(rows, cols, lambda)\fR \(-> the branches' type
MAKEARRAY(rows, cols, LAMBDA(r, c, body)): the body over the categories rows \[u00D7] cols, with r and c the item positions
.TP
\fBBYROW(array OVER C, lambda)\fR \(-> the branches' type
BYROW(array OVER C, LAMBDA(row, body)): the body per item of array's other categories, row being the values along C (the body reduces it: SUM(row), \[u2026]) (also \fBBYCOL\fR)
.TP
\fBMAP(array1, \[u2026], lambda)\fR \(-> the branches' type
MAP(array1, \[u2026], LAMBDA(p, \[u2026], body)): the body applied element by element
