.TP
\fBCHOLESKY(A OVER R, C INTO R2, C2)\fR \(-> number
CHOLESKY(A OVER R, C INTO R2, C2): the lower-triangular L with L\[u00B7]L\[u1D40] = A for a symmetric positive-definite A (asymmetric pairs averaged), row by row; #NUM! where A is not positive definite
.TP
\fBEIGEN(A OVER R, C INTO R2, C2)\fR \(-> number
EIGEN(A OVER R, C INTO R2, C2): for a symmetric A (asymmetric pairs averaged), its eigenvalues largest magnitude first, then the matrix of their unit eigenvectors as columns: (n + 1) \[u00D7] n values, row by row
.TP
\fBFOURIER(y OVER T, [inverse] INTO K)\fR \(-> text
FOURIER(y OVER T, [inverse] INTO K): Gnumeric's discrete Fourier transform (scaled by 1/n, zero-padded to a power of two), each value as complex text "a+bi"
